#: conf.json:summary
msgid "Names, binding, capture-avoiding substitution, rewriting and lambda-calculus normalizers shared by Luna Flow's symbolic packages."
msgstr "为 Luna Flow 各符号计算包共享的名字、绑定、避免捕获的代换、重写以及 λ 演算范式化器。"

#: manual/api/adapter.md:1
msgid "adapter API"
msgstr "adapter API"

#: manual/api/adapter.md:3
msgid "The `adapter` package has no public items. It is a contract-test package: its white-box tests define a small downstream-style AST, implement `@syntax.BindingSyntax` for it, and check that generic substitution and generic rewriting behave as documented on an AST that is not `Term[T]`."
msgstr "`adapter` 包没有公开项。它是一个契约测试包：其白盒测试定义了一个小型的、下游风格的 AST，为其实现 `@syntax.BindingSyntax`，并检查泛型代换与泛型重写在一个不是 `Term[T]` 的 AST 上的行为与文档一致。"

#: manual/api/adapter.md:22
msgid "The interface you implement to adapt your own AST is [`@syntax.BindingSyntax`](syntax.md); the algorithms you then get are [`@syntax.generic_free_variables`](syntax.md), [`@substitution.GenericSubstitution`](substitution.md) and [`@rewrite.generic_top_down_once`](rewrite.md). The contract is explained in the [adapter design](../design/adapter.md), and the [adapter tutorial](../tutorial/adapter.md) builds an adapter step by step."
msgstr "为适配你自己的 AST 而需实现的接口是 [`@syntax.BindingSyntax`](syntax.md)；随后你将获得的算法是 [`@syntax.generic_free_variables`](syntax.md)、[`@substitution.GenericSubstitution`](substitution.md) 和 [`@rewrite.generic_top_down_once`](rewrite.md)。该契约在 [adapter 设计](../design/adapter.md)中说明，[adapter 教程](../tutorial/adapter.md)则一步步构建一个适配器。"

#: manual/api/adapter.md:30
msgid "What the tests check"
msgstr "测试检查的内容"

#: manual/api/adapter.md:32
msgid "The test file `src/adapter/poly_adapter_wbtest.mbt` uses a private AST with four node kinds: integer literals (projected as `Opaque`), variables, an n-ary sum node (projected as `Apply`) and a scope node (projected as `Bind`). It checks that"
msgstr "测试文件 `src/adapter/poly_adapter_wbtest.mbt` 使用一个包含四种节点的私有 AST：整数字面量（投影为 `Opaque`）、变量、n 元求和节点（投影为 `Apply`）以及作用域节点（投影为 `Bind`）。它检查"

#: manual/api/adapter.md:37
msgid "`GenericSubstitution::apply_once` substitutes simultaneously and in one pass: $\\{x \\mapsto y,\\ y \\mapsto 2\\}$ applied to $x + y$ gives $y + 2$;"
msgstr "`GenericSubstitution::apply_once` 同时且一趟完成代换：将 $\\{x \\mapsto y,\\ y \\mapsto 2\\}$ 作用于 $x + y$ 得到 $y + 2$；"

#: manual/api/adapter.md:39
msgid "substitution leaves variables outside its domain in place (partial evaluation);"
msgstr "代换保留其定义域之外的变量不变（部分求值）；"

#: manual/api/adapter.md:41
msgid "`generic_top_down_once` finds a redex inside an argument, rebuilds the parent through the trait constructors, and reports the path `[ApplyArgument(0)]`."
msgstr "`generic_top_down_once` 在某个参数内部找到可约式，通过 trait 构造器重建父节点，并报告路径 `[ApplyArgument(0)]`。"

#: manual/api/core.md:1
msgid "core API"
msgstr "core API"

#: manual/api/core.md:3
msgid "The `core` package defines the vocabulary that every other package of `type_theory` shares: variable names, fresh-name generation, ordered scopes, telescopes and finite renamings. All values are immutable: every operation that \"changes\" a value returns a new one and leaves its argument untouched."
msgstr "`core` 包定义了 `type_theory` 中所有其他包共享的基本词汇：变量名、新名字生成、有序作用域、伸缩式（telescope）以及有限重命名。所有值都是不可变的：每个“改变”值的操作都返回一个新值，并保持其参数不变。"

#: manual/api/core.md:8
msgid "Import it in `moon.pkg`:"
msgstr "在 `moon.pkg` 中导入它："

#: manual/api/core.md:16
msgid "The examples below also use `moonbitlang/core/immut/hashset` for name sets. The mathematics behind these definitions is in the [core design](../design/core.md)."
msgstr "下面的示例还使用 `moonbitlang/core/immut/hashset` 表示名字集合。这些定义背后的数学见 [core 设计](../design/core.md)。"

#: manual/api/core.md:19
msgid "Names"
msgstr "名字"

#: manual/api/core.md:23
msgid "`Name` is a variable name, compared by its text."
msgstr "`Name` 是变量名，按其文本进行比较。"

#: manual/api/core.md:31
msgid "Two names are the same variable exactly when their texts are equal. A name carries no scope, no unique identifier and no type: binding is decided by the syntax that contains the name. The field `text` is read-only outside the package; use `Name::new` and `Name::text`."
msgstr "两个名字当且仅当文本相等时才是同一个变量。名字不携带作用域、唯一标识符或类型：绑定关系由包含该名字的语法决定。字段 `text` 在包外是只读的；请使用 `Name::new` 和 `Name::text`。"

#: manual/api/core.md:38
msgid "`Name::new` makes a name from its text."
msgstr "`Name::new` 由文本构造一个名字。"

#: manual/api/core.md:44
msgid "Any string is accepted, including the empty string and strings that look like generated names such as `x_1`. The library never parses the text, except that `fresh_name` appends `_<k>` suffixes to it."
msgstr "任何字符串都可接受，包括空字符串以及看起来像生成名字的字符串，例如 `x_1`。库从不解析该文本，只是 `fresh_name` 会在其后追加 `_<k>` 后缀。"

#: manual/api/core.md:50
msgid "`Name::text` returns the text of a name."
msgstr "`Name::text` 返回名字的文本。"

#: manual/api/core.md:67
msgid "These methods compare and hash names through their text."
msgstr "这些方法通过名字的文本对其进行比较和哈希。"

#: manual/api/core.md:75
msgid "They are the `Eq`, `Compare` and `Hash` implementations promoted to methods. `compare` is the order of `String` on the texts: shorter texts first, then by UTF-16 code units. It is a total order, so names can be sorted for deterministic output; `hash` lets names live in `HashSet` and `HashMap`. Prefer the operators `==`, `!=`, `<` and friends in new code."
msgstr "它们是提升为方法的 `Eq`、`Compare` 和 `Hash` 实现。`compare` 是文本上 `String` 的顺序：较短的文本在前，然后按 UTF-16 码元比较。这是一个全序，因此可以对名字排序以获得确定性输出；`hash` 使名字可以放入 `HashSet` 和 `HashMap`。新代码中请优先使用运算符 `==`、`!=`、`<` 等。"

#: manual/api/core.md:93
msgid "`fresh_name` returns a name that does not occur in a set of used names, keeping a hint when possible."
msgstr "`fresh_name` 返回一个不在已用名字集合中出现的名字，并在可能时保留提示名。"

#: manual/api/core.md:100
msgid "`fresh_name(hint, used)` returns `hint` itself when `hint` is not in `used`. Otherwise it tries `hint_1`, `hint_2`, … in order and returns the first candidate that is not in `used`. The result is a function of `hint` and `used` only, so repeated runs produce the same names. It always terminates: at most $|used| + 1$ candidates are tried."
msgstr "当 `hint` 不在 `used` 中时，`fresh_name(hint, used)` 直接返回 `hint`。否则它依次尝试 `hint_1`、`hint_2`、…，并返回第一个不在 `used` 中的候选。结果只依赖于 `hint` 和 `used`，因此重复运行会产生相同的名字。它总会终止：最多尝试 $|used| + 1$ 个候选。"

#: manual/api/core.md:115
msgid "Scopes"
msgstr "作用域"

#: manual/api/core.md:119
msgid "`Context` is an ordered list of names in scope, innermost last."
msgstr "`Context` 是作用域内名字的有序列表，最内层的在最后。"

#: manual/api/core.md:127
msgid "A context may contain the same name more than once; a later entry shadows an earlier one. Two contexts are equal when they list the same names in the same order."
msgstr "一个上下文可以多次包含同一个名字；较后的条目遮蔽较早的条目。两个上下文当以相同顺序列出相同名字时相等。"

#: manual/api/core.md:133
msgid "These functions build a context with no names, or with the names of an array in order."
msgstr "这些函数构造一个不含名字的上下文，或按顺序包含某个数组中名字的上下文。"

#: manual/api/core.md:141
msgid "`from_array` copies the array, so later changes to the array do not affect the context."
msgstr "`from_array` 会复制数组，因此之后对数组的修改不会影响上下文。"

#: manual/api/core.md:146
msgid "`Context::extend_with` returns the context with one more name at the inner end."
msgstr "`Context::extend_with` 返回在内层末端多一个名字的上下文。"

#: manual/api/core.md:153
msgid "The original context is unchanged. The call copies the names, so it costs $O(n)$ for a context of length $n$."
msgstr "原上下文保持不变。该调用会复制名字，因此对长度为 $n$ 的上下文开销为 $O(n)$。"

#: manual/api/core.md:158
msgid "These methods query a context."
msgstr "这些方法查询上下文。"

#: manual/api/core.md:167
msgid "`contains` is a linear search. `to_array` returns a copy, outermost name first. `equal` is the promoted `Eq` implementation."
msgstr "`contains` 是线性查找。`to_array` 返回一个副本，最外层名字在前。`equal` 是提升的 `Eq` 实现。"

#: manual/api/core.md:184
msgid "`Telescope[T]` is a sequence of binders, each with an annotation of type `T`, in dependency order."
msgstr "`Telescope[T]` 是按依赖顺序排列的绑定子序列，每个绑定子带有一个类型为 `T` 的标注。"

#: manual/api/core.md:193
msgid "In a telescope $x_1 : A_1, \\dots, x_n : A_n$ the annotation $A_i$ may refer to $x_1, \\dots, x_{i-1}$. `Telescope` records the order; it does not check what the annotations mention."
msgstr "在伸缩式 $x_1 : A_1, \\dots, x_n : A_n$ 中，标注 $A_i$ 可以引用 $x_1, \\dots, x_{i-1}$。`Telescope` 只记录顺序；它不检查标注中提及了什么。"

#: manual/api/core.md:199
msgid "These functions build and read a telescope."
msgstr "这些函数构造和读取伸缩式。"

#: manual/api/core.md:209
msgid "`extend_with` appends one binder and returns a new telescope; `to_array` returns a copy of the entries, first binder first."
msgstr "`extend_with` 追加一个绑定子并返回新的伸缩式；`to_array` 返回条目的副本，第一个绑定子在前。"

#: manual/api/core.md:224
#: manual/design/core.md:55
msgid "Renamings"
msgstr "重命名"

#: manual/api/core.md:228
msgid "`Renaming` is a finite map from names to names; names outside its domain are left unchanged."
msgstr "`Renaming` 是从名字到名字的有限映射；定义域之外的名字保持不变。"

#: manual/api/core.md:237
msgid "A renaming $\\rho$ denotes the total function $\\rho(n) = m$ if $(n, m)$ is an entry and $\\rho(n) = n$ otherwise. It is applied simultaneously: the image of a name is never renamed again. A renaming need not be injective. Equality (`Renaming::equal`) compares the entry lists, so two renamings that denote the same function can still be different values."
msgstr "重命名 $\\rho$ 表示如下全函数：若 $(n, m)$ 是一个条目则 $\\rho(n) = m$，否则 $\\rho(n) = n$。它是同时作用的：名字的像不会再次被重命名。重命名不必是单射。相等性（`Renaming::equal`）比较的是条目列表，因此表示同一函数的两个重命名仍可能是不同的值。"

#: manual/api/core.md:245
msgid "These functions build renamings."
msgstr "这些函数构造重命名。"

#: manual/api/core.md:253
msgid "`set(from, to_)` adds the entry `from ↦ to_`, replacing an existing image of `from` in place."
msgstr "`set(from, to_)` 添加条目 `from ↦ to_`，若 `from` 已有像则就地替换。"

#: manual/api/core.md:258
msgid "`Renaming::apply` returns the image of a name."
msgstr "`Renaming::apply` 返回名字的像。"

#: manual/api/core.md:266
msgid "`Renaming::without` removes a name from the domain."
msgstr "`Renaming::without` 从定义域中移除一个名字。"

#: manual/api/core.md:272
msgid "This is the operation a binder performs: under a binder for `x`, free occurrences of `x` are no longer the `x` of the renaming."
msgstr "这正是绑定子所执行的操作：在 `x` 的绑定子之下，`x` 的自由出现不再是该重命名中的 `x`。"

#: manual/api/core.md:277
msgid "These methods return the names a renaming mentions."
msgstr "这些方法返回重命名中提及的名字。"

#: manual/api/core.md:284
msgid "`support` contains every source and every target of an entry; `targets` contains only the targets. Capture-avoiding operations use them to choose fresh binder names."
msgstr "`support` 包含每个条目的所有源和所有目标；`targets` 只包含目标。避免捕获的操作用它们来选择新的绑定子名字。"

#: manual/api/core.md:290
msgid "`Renaming::then` composes two renamings, applying `self` first."
msgstr "`Renaming::then` 复合两个重命名，先应用 `self`。"

#: manual/api/core.md:296
msgid "For every name $n$, `r.then(s).apply(n) == s.apply(r.apply(n))`."
msgstr "对每个名字 $n$，`r.then(s).apply(n) == s.apply(r.apply(n))`。"

#: manual/api/core.md:316
msgid "`Renaming::equal` compares two renamings entry by entry."
msgstr "`Renaming::equal` 逐条目比较两个重命名。"

#: manual/api/core.md:322
#: manual/api/eval.md:52
msgid "It is the promoted `Eq` implementation; use `==` in new code."
msgstr "它是提升的 `Eq` 实现；新代码中请使用 `==`。"

#: manual/api/core.md:324
#: manual/api/core.md:326
#: manual/api/stlc.md:259
#: manual/api/stlc.md:261
#: manual/api/syntax.md:319
#: manual/api/syntax.md:321
msgid "Deprecated"
msgstr "已弃用"

#: manual/api/core.md:326
#: manual/api/stlc.md:261
#: manual/api/syntax.md:321
msgid "Replacement"
msgstr "替代项"

#: manual/api/core.md:331
msgid "`extend` became a reserved word in MoonBit 0.10, so the methods were renamed. The old names remain as deprecated aliases. The method forms `not_equal`, `op_lt`, `op_le`, `op_gt`, `op_ge`, `hash_combine` and `to_repr` on these types are hidden and deprecated; use the operators `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, the `Hash` trait and `Repr(x)` instead."
msgstr "`extend` 在 MoonBit 0.10 中成为保留字，因此这些方法被重命名。旧名字作为已弃用的别名保留。这些类型上的方法形式 `not_equal`、`op_lt`、`op_le`、`op_gt`、`op_ge`、`hash_combine` 和 `to_repr` 已被隐藏并弃用；请改用运算符 `!=`、`<`、`<=`、`>`、`>=`、`Hash` trait 以及 `Repr(x)`。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:1
msgid "debruijn API"
msgstr "debruijn API"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:3
msgid "The `debruijn` package represents bound variables by De Bruijn indices: `Bound(i)` refers to the binder `i` levels up. It converts from and to named syntax, checks scope, shifts and substitutes indices, and implements leftmost-outermost beta reduction without any renaming. Free variables stay named."
msgstr "`debruijn` 包用 De Bruijn 索引表示约束变量：`Bound(i)` 指向向上第 `i` 层的绑定子。它在 De Bruijn 语法与具名语法之间相互转换，检查作用域，对索引进行移位和代换，并实现无需任何重命名的最左最外 β-归约。自由变量保持具名。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:18
msgid "The definitions of shifting and instantiation, with derivations of their properties, are in the [debruijn design](../design/debruijn.md)."
msgstr "移位与实例化的定义及其性质的推导见 [debruijn 设计](../design/debruijn.md)。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:21
msgid "Terms and errors"
msgstr "项与错误"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:25
msgid "`DbTerm[T]` is lambda syntax with nameless binders."
msgstr "`DbTerm[T]` 是带无名绑定子的 λ 语法。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:37
msgid "`Value(v)` is a domain constant, opaque as in `@syntax.Term`."
msgstr "`Value(v)` 是领域常量，与 `@syntax.Term` 中一样是不透明的。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:38
msgid "`Free(x)` is a free variable, kept by name."
msgstr "`Free(x)` 是自由变量，按名字保存。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:39
msgid "`Bound(i)` refers to the `i`-th enclosing `Bind`, counting from 0 for the innermost."
msgstr "`Bound(i)` 指向第 `i` 个外围 `Bind`，最内层从 0 开始计数。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:41
msgid "`Apply(head, args)` is n-ary application, read as a curried spine."
msgstr "`Apply(head, args)` 是 n 元应用，按柯里化的脊（spine）来理解。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:42
msgid "`Bind(body)` is a binder; its variable is `Bound(0)` in `body`."
msgstr "`Bind(body)` 是绑定子；其变量在 `body` 中为 `Bound(0)`。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:44
msgid "A term is *well scoped* when every `Bound(i)` lies under more than `i` binders. Because binders carry no names, `==` (`DbTerm::equal`) on well-scoped terms is alpha-equivalence."
msgstr "当每个 `Bound(i)` 都位于多于 `i` 个绑定子之下时，称该项是*良作用域的*。由于绑定子不携带名字，良作用域项上的 `==`（`DbTerm::equal`）就是 α-等价。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:50
msgid "`DbTerm::equal` compares two terms structurally."
msgstr "`DbTerm::equal` 按结构比较两个项。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:58
msgid "`ScopeError` describes an index that does not refer to a binder."
msgstr "`ScopeError` 描述一个不指向任何绑定子的索引。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:69
msgid "`UnboundIndex(index, depth)`: `Bound(index)` occurs under only `depth` binders."
msgstr "`UnboundIndex(index, depth)`：`Bound(index)` 仅出现在 `depth` 个绑定子之下。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:71
msgid "`NegativeIndex(index)`: a negative index."
msgstr "`NegativeIndex(index)`：负索引。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:72
msgid "`NegativeShift(index, delta, cutoff)`: shifting `Bound(index)` by `delta` would make it negative; `cutoff` is the effective cutoff at the occurrence."
msgstr "`NegativeShift(index, delta, cutoff)`：将 `Bound(index)` 移位 `delta` 会使其变为负数；`cutoff` 是该出现处的有效截断值。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:75
msgid "Conversion and validation"
msgstr "转换与验证"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:79
msgid "`from_named` converts named syntax to De Bruijn syntax."
msgstr "`from_named` 将具名语法转换为 De Bruijn 语法。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:85
msgid "A variable bound by an enclosing `Bind` becomes `Bound(i)`, where `i` counts the binders between the occurrence and its binder (the nearest binder of that name wins). Free variables become `Free`. The result is always well scoped, and alpha-equivalent named terms give equal results."
msgstr "由外围 `Bind` 绑定的变量变为 `Bound(i)`，其中 `i` 计数该出现与其绑定子之间的绑定子个数（同名时最近的绑定子胜出）。自由变量变为 `Free`。结果总是良作用域的，且 α-等价的具名项给出相等的结果。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:92
msgid "`to_named` converts De Bruijn syntax back to named syntax with deterministic binder names."
msgstr "`to_named` 将 De Bruijn 语法转换回具名语法，并使用确定性的绑定子名字。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:99
msgid "Binders are named `x`, `x_1`, `x_2`, …: each one gets the first name of that sequence that is neither a free name of the term nor the name of an enclosing binder. Returns `Err(NegativeIndex)` or `Err(UnboundIndex)` for an ill-scoped term. For a well-scoped `d`, `from_named(to_named(d))` is `d`; for a named `t`, `to_named(from_named(t))` is alpha-equivalent to `t`."
msgstr "绑定子依次命名为 `x`、`x_1`、`x_2`、…：每个绑定子取该序列中第一个既不是项的自由名字、也不是外围绑定子名字的名字。对作用域不良的项返回 `Err(NegativeIndex)` 或 `Err(UnboundIndex)`。对良作用域的 `d`，`from_named(to_named(d))` 就是 `d`；对具名项 `t`，`to_named(from_named(t))` 与 `t` α-等价。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:122
msgid "The binder becomes `x_1` because `x` is a free name of the term."
msgstr "绑定子变为 `x_1`，因为 `x` 是该项的自由名字。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:126
msgid "`validate` checks that every bound index refers to an enclosing binder."
msgstr "`validate` 检查每个约束索引都指向某个外围绑定子。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:132
msgid "Returns `Ok(())` for a well-scoped term and otherwise the first error found in pre-order."
msgstr "对良作用域项返回 `Ok(())`，否则返回按前序遍历找到的第一个错误。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:144
msgid "Index operations"
msgstr "索引操作"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:148
msgid "`shift` adds `delta` to every index that is free relative to a cutoff."
msgstr "`shift` 将 `delta` 加到每个相对于截断值为自由的索引上。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:154
msgid "`shift(t, delta, cutoff)` is the operation $\\uparrow^{delta}_{cutoff}$: under `k` binders, an index `i >= cutoff + k` becomes `i + delta`, and smaller indices are left alone. Returns `Err(NegativeShift)` if an index would become negative and `Err(NegativeIndex)` if the input contains a negative index."
msgstr "`shift(t, delta, cutoff)` 即操作 $\\uparrow^{delta}_{cutoff}$：在 `k` 个绑定子之下，索引 `i >= cutoff + k` 变为 `i + delta`，较小的索引保持不变。若某索引会变为负数则返回 `Err(NegativeShift)`，若输入包含负索引则返回 `Err(NegativeIndex)`。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:161
msgid "`substitute_bound` replaces a free index by a term."
msgstr "`substitute_bound` 用一个项替换一个自由索引。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:167
msgid "`substitute_bound(t, j, s)` is $[j \\mapsto s]\\,t$: under `k` binders, `Bound(j + k)` is replaced by `s` shifted up by `k`, so that the free indices of `s` keep pointing at the same binders. Other indices are unchanged; the binder count of the result is not adjusted. Returns `Err(NegativeIndex)` for a negative `j` or a negative index in `t`. It does not check for unbound indices; use `validate` for that."
msgstr "`substitute_bound(t, j, s)` 即 $[j \\mapsto s]\\,t$：在 `k` 个绑定子之下，`Bound(j + k)` 被替换为向上移位 `k` 的 `s`，使 `s` 的自由索引仍指向相同的绑定子。其他索引不变；结果的绑定子计数不作调整。对负的 `j` 或 `t` 中的负索引返回 `Err(NegativeIndex)`。它不检查未绑定的索引；请使用 `validate` 进行检查。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:176
msgid "`instantiate` opens a binder body with an argument."
msgstr "`instantiate` 用一个实参打开绑定子的体。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:182
msgid "`instantiate(body, arg)` computes $\\uparrow^{-1}_0\\big([0 \\mapsto \\uparrow^{1}_0 arg]\\,body\\big)$, the result of the beta step $(\\lambda.\\,body)\\,arg$. On well-scoped input it never returns an error."
msgstr "`instantiate(body, arg)` 计算 $\\uparrow^{-1}_0\\big([0 \\mapsto \\uparrow^{1}_0 arg]\\,body\\big)$，即 β 步 $(\\lambda.\\,body)\\,arg$ 的结果。在良作用域输入上它从不返回错误。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:209
msgid "Reduction"
msgstr "归约"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:213
msgid "`DbStepResult[T]` is the outcome of one De Bruijn reduction attempt."
msgstr "`DbStepResult[T]` 是一次 De Bruijn 归约尝试的结果。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:224
msgid "`NoStep` and `Reduced` have the meaning of `@rewrite.StepResult`; the rule name is always `\"beta\"`. `ScopeFailure` reports an index error met while contracting a redex."
msgstr "`NoStep` 和 `Reduced` 的含义与 `@rewrite.StepResult` 相同；规则名总是 `\"beta\"`。`ScopeFailure` 报告在收缩可约式时遇到的索引错误。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:230
msgid "`reduce_once` performs one leftmost-outermost beta step."
msgstr "`reduce_once` 执行一步最左最外 β 归约。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:236
msgid "A redex is `Apply(Bind(body), [a, ..rest])`; it becomes `instantiate(body, a)`, applied to `rest` if `rest` is not empty. The search order is the root, then the head, then the arguments from left to right, and binder bodies are entered. `reduce_once` does not validate its input: call `validate` first if the term may be ill scoped."
msgstr "可约式形如 `Apply(Bind(body), [a, ..rest])`；它变为 `instantiate(body, a)`，若 `rest` 非空则再应用于 `rest`。搜索顺序为：根，然后头部，然后从左到右的各参数，并且会进入绑定子的体。`reduce_once` 不验证其输入：如果项可能作用域不良，请先调用 `validate`。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:244
msgid "`DbNormalizationResult[T]` is the outcome of bounded De Bruijn normalization."
msgstr "`DbNormalizationResult[T]` 是有界 De Bruijn 范式化的结果。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:255
msgid "`ScopeFailure` carries the term on which the failing step was attempted and the number of steps taken before it."
msgstr "`ScopeFailure` 携带尝试失败步骤时所在的项，以及在此之前已执行的步数。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:260
msgid "`normalize` repeats `reduce_once` until no step applies, a step fails, or a step limit is reached."
msgstr "`normalize` 重复执行 `reduce_once`，直到没有可执行的步骤、某一步失败或达到步数上限。"

#: manual/api/debruijn.md:267
msgid "It has the step-count contract of `@rewrite.normalize`: at most `max_steps` steps, and one extra `reduce_once` call to classify the final term."
msgstr "它遵循 `@rewrite.normalize` 的步数契约：最多 `max_steps` 步，并额外调用一次 `reduce_once` 来判定最终项。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:1
msgid "eval API"
msgstr "eval API"

#: manual/api/eval.md:3
msgid "The `eval` package names the usual reduction strategies and runs any rewrite rule with one of them: one step, bounded normalization, or a full trace. It is a thin layer over [rewrite](rewrite.md); the rule itself (beta, eta, a domain simplification) is supplied by the caller."
msgstr "`eval` 包为常见的归约策略命名，并用其中一种策略运行任意重写规则：单步、有界范式化或完整轨迹。它是 [rewrite](rewrite.md) 之上的一层薄封装；规则本身（β、η 或某个领域化简）由调用者提供。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:16
msgid "The examples use the beta rule of `Luna-Flow/type_theory/utlc/lambda` (alias `@lambda`). The strategies are defined precisely in the [eval design](../design/eval.md)."
msgstr "示例使用 `Luna-Flow/type_theory/utlc/lambda`（别名 `@lambda`）的 β 规则。这些策略的精确定义见 [eval 设计](../design/eval.md)。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:22
msgid "`Strategy` selects where the next step is taken."
msgstr "`Strategy` 选择下一步发生的位置。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:33
#: manual/semantics.md:44
msgid "Strategy"
msgstr "策略"

#: manual/api/eval.md:33
msgid "Next position"
msgstr "下一个位置"

#: manual/api/eval.md:33
msgid "Enters binders and arguments"
msgstr "是否进入绑定子和参数"

#: manual/api/eval.md:35
msgid "leftmost-outermost redex (`@rewrite.top_down_once`)"
msgstr "最左最外可约式（`@rewrite.top_down_once`）"

#: manual/api/eval.md:35
#: manual/api/eval.md:36
#: manual/api/eval.md:38
msgid "yes"
msgstr "是"

#: manual/api/eval.md:36
msgid "leftmost-innermost redex (`@rewrite.bottom_up_once`)"
msgstr "最左最内可约式（`@rewrite.bottom_up_once`）"

#: manual/api/eval.md:37
msgid "the root, else the head of an application, recursively"
msgstr "根，否则为应用的头部，递归进行"

#: manual/api/eval.md:37
msgid "no"
msgstr "否"

#: manual/api/eval.md:38
msgid "same as `NormalOrder`"
msgstr "与 `NormalOrder` 相同"

#: manual/api/eval.md:40
msgid "`FullNormal` currently selects the same traversal as `NormalOrder`; it names the intent \"reduce to full normal form\" and may diverge from `NormalOrder` if another full-normalization traversal is added."
msgstr "`FullNormal` 目前选择与 `NormalOrder` 相同的遍历；它表达“归约到完全范式”的意图，若将来加入另一种完全范式化遍历，则可能与 `NormalOrder` 不同。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:46
msgid "`Strategy::equal` compares two strategies."
msgstr "`Strategy::equal` 比较两个策略。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:56
msgid "`reduce_once` performs at most one reduction step with a strategy."
msgstr "`reduce_once` 使用某个策略执行至多一步归约。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:62
msgid "The result follows the contract of `@rewrite.StepResult`: `Reduced` reports one rewritten position and its path. For `NormalOrder`, `FullNormal` and `ApplicativeOrder`, `NoStep` means the rule applies nowhere. For `WeakHead`, `NoStep` means the rule applies neither at the root nor at any head position of the application spine; the term is then in weak head normal form for the rule, but may contain redexes under binders or in arguments."
msgstr "结果遵循 `@rewrite.StepResult` 的契约：`Reduced` 报告一个被重写的位置及其路径。对于 `NormalOrder`、`FullNormal` 和 `ApplicativeOrder`，`NoStep` 表示规则在任何位置都不适用。对于 `WeakHead`，`NoStep` 表示规则既不适用于根，也不适用于应用脊上的任何头部位置；此时该项相对于该规则处于弱头范式，但在绑定子之下或参数中仍可能包含可约式。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:90
msgid "`evaluate` normalizes a term by repeating `reduce_once` with one strategy."
msgstr "`evaluate` 通过以某个策略重复 `reduce_once` 来范式化一个项。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:96
msgid "`evaluate(term, name, rule, strategy, max_steps)` is `@rewrite.normalize(term, t => reduce_once(t, name, rule, strategy), max_steps)`, with the same step-count contract: at most `max_steps` steps, and `NormalForm` only for a term on which the strategy finds no step."
msgstr "`evaluate(term, name, rule, strategy, max_steps)` 即 `@rewrite.normalize(term, t => reduce_once(t, name, rule, strategy), max_steps)`，具有相同的步数契约：最多 `max_steps` 步，且仅当策略在某个项上找不到步骤时才返回 `NormalForm`。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:123
msgid "`trace` normalizes like `evaluate` and records every step."
msgstr "`trace` 像 `evaluate` 一样范式化，并记录每一步。"

#: manual/api/eval.md:129
msgid "It is `@rewrite.trace` with the step function of the strategy. The trace satisfies the chaining invariants of `@rewrite.ReductionTrace`."
msgstr "它就是带有该策略步进函数的 `@rewrite.trace`。该轨迹满足 `@rewrite.ReductionTrace` 的链接不变式。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:1
msgid "rewrite API"
msgstr "rewrite API"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:3
msgid "The `rewrite` package applies a rewrite rule at one position of a term and reports exactly what happened: the term before and after, the rule's name and the path from the root to the rewritten position. Bounded normalization and traces are built by repeating such single steps. Every function has a `Term[T]` version and, where noted, a version for any `@syntax.BindingSyntax` AST."
msgstr "`rewrite` 包在项的某一个位置应用一条重写规则，并准确报告发生了什么：之前与之后的项、规则名，以及从根到被重写位置的路径。有界范式化与轨迹都是通过重复这样的单步构建的。每个函数都有 `Term[T]` 版本，并在注明处提供适用于任意 `@syntax.BindingSyntax` AST 的版本。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:17
msgid "A *rule* is a function `(Term[T]) -> Term[T]?` that returns `Some(result)` when it applies to a term as a whole and `None` otherwise. The traversal functions decide *where* the rule is tried. The theory is in the [rewrite design](../design/rewrite.md)."
msgstr "*规则*是一个函数 `(Term[T]) -> Term[T]?`，当它作为整体适用于某个项时返回 `Some(result)`，否则返回 `None`。遍历函数决定在*何处*尝试规则。相关理论见 [rewrite 设计](../design/rewrite.md)。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:22
msgid "Rule names"
msgstr "规则名"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:26
msgid "`RuleName` is a non-empty identifier for a reduction rule."
msgstr "`RuleName` 是归约规则的非空标识符。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:34
msgid "Rule names label steps in results and traces. They compare, order and hash by their text; the order is that of `String`: shorter texts first, then by UTF-16 code units."
msgstr "规则名用于在结果和轨迹中标记步骤。它们按文本进行比较、排序和哈希；顺序为 `String` 的顺序：较短的文本在前，然后按 UTF-16 码元比较。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:40
msgid "`RuleName::new` validates and creates a rule name."
msgstr "`RuleName::new` 验证并创建一个规则名。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:46
msgid "Returns `Err(RuleNameError::Empty)` for the empty string and `Ok(name)` otherwise."
msgstr "对空字符串返回 `Err(RuleNameError::Empty)`，否则返回 `Ok(name)`。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:51
msgid "`RuleName::unsafe_new` creates a rule name from a string known to be non-empty."
msgstr "`RuleName::unsafe_new` 从已知非空的字符串创建规则名。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:58
msgid "Aborts on the empty string. Use it for literals such as `\"beta\"`, where the invariant is evident; use `RuleName::new` for names that come from input."
msgstr "遇到空字符串时中止。对 `\"beta\"` 这类不变式显而易见的字面量使用它；对来自输入的名字使用 `RuleName::new`。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:63
msgid "`RuleName::value` returns the text of a rule name."
msgstr "`RuleName::value` 返回规则名的文本。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:71
msgid "These methods are the promoted `Eq`, `Compare` and `Hash` implementations."
msgstr "这些方法是提升的 `Eq`、`Compare` 和 `Hash` 实现。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:94
msgid "`RuleNameError` lists the reasons a rule name is invalid."
msgstr "`RuleNameError` 列出规则名无效的原因。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:103
msgid "`Empty` is the only case: rule names must not be empty."
msgstr "`Empty` 是唯一的情形：规则名不得为空。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:105
msgid "Positions"
msgstr "位置"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:109
msgid "`ReductionFrame` is one step from a node to one of its children."
msgstr "`ReductionFrame` 是从一个节点到其某个子节点的一步。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:120
msgid "`BinderBody` enters the body of a `Bind`, `ApplyHead` the head of an `Apply`, and `ApplyArgument(i)` its argument number `i`, counting from 0."
msgstr "`BinderBody` 进入 `Bind` 的体，`ApplyHead` 进入 `Apply` 的头部，`ApplyArgument(i)` 进入其第 `i` 个参数（从 0 开始计数）。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:125
msgid "`ReductionPath` is the sequence of frames from the root to a position."
msgstr "`ReductionPath` 是从根到某个位置的帧序列。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:133
msgid "The empty path is the root."
msgstr "空路径即根。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:137
msgid "These functions build and read paths."
msgstr "这些函数构造和读取路径。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:145
msgid "`prepend(frame)` adds a frame at the root end, which is how a traversal lifts the path of a step in a child to the parent. `to_array` returns the frames root first."
msgstr "`prepend(frame)` 在根端添加一帧，遍历正是借此把子节点中某一步的路径提升到父节点。`to_array` 返回以根开头的帧。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:151
msgid "`ReductionPath::equal` compares two paths frame by frame."
msgstr "`ReductionPath::equal` 逐帧比较两条路径。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:167
msgid "Single steps on `Term`"
msgstr "`Term` 上的单步"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:171
msgid "`StepResult[T]` is the outcome of one reduction attempt."
msgstr "`StepResult[T]` 是一次归约尝试的结果。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:181
msgid "`NoStep` means the traversal found no position where the rule applies. `Reduced` records the whole term `before`, the whole term `after`, the rule and the path of the rewritten position. Exactly one position was rewritten: the subterm of `before` at `path` is a redex of the rule, and `after` is `before` with that subterm replaced by the rule's result."
msgstr "`NoStep` 表示遍历没有找到规则适用的位置。`Reduced` 记录整个项 `before`、整个项 `after`、规则以及被重写位置的路径。恰好有一个位置被重写：`before` 在 `path` 处的子项是该规则的可约式，而 `after` 是将该子项替换为规则结果后的 `before`。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:189
msgid "`top_down_once` rewrites the first position, in pre-order, at which the rule applies."
msgstr "`top_down_once` 按前序重写规则适用的第一个位置。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:196
msgid "The rule is tried at a node before its children; children are visited head first, then arguments from left to right, and binder bodies are entered. The chosen position is the leftmost-outermost redex. `NoStep` means that the rule applies nowhere in the term."
msgstr "规则先在节点本身上尝试，再在其子节点上尝试；子节点的访问顺序是先头部，再从左到右依次访问参数，并且会进入绑定子的体。所选位置是最左最外的可约式。`NoStep` 表示该规则在项中任何位置都不适用。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:203
msgid "`bottom_up_once` rewrites the first position, in post-order, at which the rule applies."
msgstr "`bottom_up_once` 按后序遍历，改写规则适用的第一个位置。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:210
msgid "Children are tried before their parent, in the same left-to-right order. The chosen position is the leftmost-innermost redex. `NoStep` again means that the rule applies nowhere."
msgstr "子节点先于其父节点尝试，顺序同样是从左到右。所选位置是最左最内的可约式。`NoStep` 同样表示该规则在任何位置都不适用。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:243
msgid "Repeating steps on `Term`"
msgstr "在 `Term` 上重复执行步骤"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:247
msgid "`NormalizationResult[T]` is the outcome of bounded repetition of a step function."
msgstr "`NormalizationResult[T]` 是对步进函数进行有界重复的结果。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:258
msgid "`NormalForm(term, steps)`: the step function returns `NoStep` on `term`, which was reached after `steps` steps. `StepLimitReached(term, steps)`: the limit of `steps` steps was used up and `term` can still be reduced."
msgstr "`NormalForm(term, steps)`：步进函数在 `term` 上返回 `NoStep`，该项是经过 `steps` 步得到的。`StepLimitReached(term, steps)`：`steps` 步的上限已用尽，且 `term` 仍可继续归约。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:264
msgid "`normalize` applies a step function until it returns `NoStep` or a step limit is reached."
msgstr "`normalize` 反复应用步进函数，直到它返回 `NoStep` 或达到步数上限。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:271
msgid "`normalize(term, step, max_steps)` performs at most `max_steps` successful steps and calls `step` at most `max_steps + 1` times: after the last allowed step it calls `step` once more to decide between `NormalForm` and `StepLimitReached`. With `max_steps <= 0` it performs no step and only classifies `term`. The step function decides the strategy; see [eval](eval.md) for ready-made ones."
msgstr "`normalize(term, step, max_steps)` 至多执行 `max_steps` 个成功步骤，并且至多调用 `step` `max_steps + 1` 次：在最后一个允许的步骤之后，它会再调用一次 `step`，以判定结果是 `NormalForm` 还是 `StepLimitReached`。当 `max_steps <= 0` 时，它不执行任何步骤，只对 `term` 进行分类。归约策略由步进函数决定；现成的步进函数见 [eval](eval.md)。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:280
msgid "`ReductionTrace[T]` records a bounded run: the initial term, every successful step and the final result."
msgstr "`ReductionTrace[T]` 记录一次有界运行：初始项、每个成功的步骤以及最终结果。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:295
msgid "Every element of `steps` is a `Reduced` value; consecutive steps chain, the `after` of one being the `before` of the next. `steps().length()` equals the `steps` count of `result`. `steps()` returns a copy."
msgstr "`steps` 中的每个元素都是一个 `Reduced` 值；相邻步骤首尾相接，前一步的 `after` 即后一步的 `before`。`steps().length()` 等于 `result` 中的 `steps` 计数。`steps()` 返回一个副本。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:301
msgid "`trace` runs the same loop as `normalize` and records every step."
msgstr "`trace` 运行与 `normalize` 相同的循环，并记录每一步。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:329
#: manual/api/syntax.md:212
msgid "Binding-aware ASTs"
msgstr "感知绑定的 AST"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:333
msgid "`GenericStepResult[N]` is `StepResult` for a downstream AST `N`."
msgstr "`GenericStepResult[N]` 是针对下游 AST `N` 的 `StepResult`。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:345
msgid "`generic_top_down_once` is `top_down_once` for any `BindingSyntax` AST."
msgstr "`generic_top_down_once` 是适用于任意 `BindingSyntax` AST 的 `top_down_once`。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:351
msgid "The traversal uses `BindingSyntax::project` to find children and the trait constructors to rebuild the parents of the rewritten node. `Opaque` and variable nodes have no children; the rule is still tried on them."
msgstr "遍历使用 `BindingSyntax::project` 查找子节点，并使用 trait 的构造函数重建被改写节点的各级父节点。`Opaque` 节点和变量节点没有子节点；规则仍会在它们上面尝试。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:357
msgid "`GenericNormalizationResult[N]` is `NormalizationResult` for a downstream AST."
msgstr "`GenericNormalizationResult[N]` 是针对下游 AST 的 `NormalizationResult`。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:370
msgid "`generic_normalize` repeats `generic_top_down_once` with one rule until no step applies or the step limit is reached."
msgstr "`generic_normalize` 使用同一条规则重复执行 `generic_top_down_once`，直到没有步骤可用或达到步数上限。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:377
msgid "It has the same step-count contract as `normalize`, with the top-down strategy fixed."
msgstr "它与 `normalize` 遵循相同的步数约定，只是策略固定为自顶向下。"

#: manual/api/rewrite.md:392
msgid "For a downstream AST see the [adapter tutorial](../tutorial/adapter.md)."
msgstr "关于下游 AST，请参阅[适配器教程](../tutorial/adapter.md)。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:1
msgid "stlc API"
msgstr "stlc API"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:3
msgid "The `stlc` package is the simply typed lambda calculus over the shared named syntax: types, signatures of typed constants, typing contexts, bidirectional type inference and checking, step-bounded operational normalization, and typed normalization by evaluation to beta-normal, eta-long form."
msgstr "`stlc` 包是基于共享命名语法的简单类型 lambda 演算：类型、带类型常量的签名、类型上下文、双向类型推断与检查、有步数上限的操作式范式化，以及到 β-范式、η-长形式的带类型求值范式化（NbE）。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:17
msgid "Terms are `@syntax.Term[Atom]`: `Bind(x, b)` is $\\lambda x.\\,b$ (without a type annotation), `Apply` is application, `Variable` a variable, and `Value` holds an `Atom`. The typing rules and the NbE algorithm are given in the [stlc design](../design/stlc.md)."
msgstr "项是 `@syntax.Term[Atom]`：`Bind(x, b)` 是 $\\lambda x.\\,b$（不带类型标注），`Apply` 是应用，`Variable` 是变量，`Value` 持有一个 `Atom`。类型规则和 NbE 算法见 [stlc 设计](../design/stlc.md)。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:22
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr "语法"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:26
msgid "`Atom` is a constant of the calculus."
msgstr "`Atom` 是该演算中的常量。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:36
msgid "`UnitLit` is the unit value $()$; `Const(c)` is a constant whose type is declared in a `Signature`."
msgstr "`UnitLit` 是单位值 $()$；`Const(c)` 是一个类型在 `Signature` 中声明的常量。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:41
msgid "`Term` is the type of STLC terms."
msgstr "`Term` 是 STLC 项的类型。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:47
msgid "It is an alias, so all of [syntax](syntax.md), [substitution](substitution.md) and [rewrite](rewrite.md) apply to STLC terms."
msgstr "它是一个别名，因此 [syntax](syntax.md)、[substitution](substitution.md) 和 [rewrite](rewrite.md) 的全部内容都适用于 STLC 项。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:52
msgid "`Ty` is a simple type."
msgstr "`Ty` 是简单类型。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:63
msgid "`Base(b)` is an uninterpreted base type, `Unit` the unit type, and `Arrow(a, b)` the function type $a \\to b$. Types are compared structurally."
msgstr "`Base(b)` 是未解释的基本类型，`Unit` 是单位类型，`Arrow(a, b)` 是函数类型 $a \\to b$。类型按结构进行比较。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:66
msgid "Signatures and contexts"
msgstr "签名与上下文"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:70
msgid "`Signature` assigns types to constants."
msgstr "`Signature` 为常量指定类型。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:84
msgid "`extend_with(c, ty)` returns a new signature with `c : ty` added; a later entry for the same name shadows an earlier one, and `lookup` returns the latest. `to_array` returns a copy of the entries in insertion order."
msgstr "`extend_with(c, ty)` 返回添加了 `c : ty` 的新签名；同名的较晚条目会遮蔽较早的条目，`lookup` 返回最新的那个。`to_array` 按插入顺序返回条目的副本。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:90
msgid "`TypeContext` assigns types to free variables."
msgstr "`TypeContext` 为自由变量指定类型。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:104
msgid "The same shadowing rule applies: the type checker extends the context when it enters a lambda, so the nearest binder of a name wins."
msgstr "同样的遮蔽规则也适用：类型检查器在进入 lambda 时扩展上下文，因此一个名字由最近的绑定子决定。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:120
msgid "Errors"
msgstr "错误"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:124
msgid "`TypeError` reports why a term is rejected."
msgstr "`TypeError` 报告项被拒绝的原因。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:140
msgid "Case"
msgstr "情形"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:140
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "含义"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:142
msgid "`x` is not in the context."
msgstr "`x` 不在上下文中。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:143
msgid "`c` is not in the signature."
msgstr "`c` 不在签名中。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:144
msgid "a lambda appears where its type must be inferred."
msgstr "lambda 出现在必须推断其类型的位置。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:145
msgid "a term of the non-function type `ty` is applied."
msgstr "对非函数类型 `ty` 的项进行了应用。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:146
msgid "the inferred type differs from the expected one."
msgstr "推断出的类型与期望的类型不同。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:147
msgid "`Apply(head, [])` has no argument."
msgstr "`Apply(head, [])` 没有参数。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:148
msgid "reserved for De Bruijn scope failures; not produced by the current functions."
msgstr "为 De Bruijn 作用域错误保留；当前的函数不会产生。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:149
msgid "an internal invariant of typed NbE failed; not expected for checked input."
msgstr "带类型 NbE 的内部不变式失败；对已检查的输入不应出现。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:151
msgid "Type checking"
msgstr "类型检查"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:155
msgid "`infer` synthesizes the type of a term."
msgstr "`infer` 合成项的类型。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:161
msgid "The unit literal has type `Unit`, constants and variables have their declared types, and an application `f a_1 … a_n` has the result type of `f` after checking each argument against the corresponding domain. A lambda alone cannot be inferred (`CannotInferLambda`). A lambda applied directly to arguments is inferred by inferring the first argument's type and the body under that assumption."
msgstr "单位字面量的类型是 `Unit`，常量和变量具有其声明的类型；对于应用 `f a_1 … a_n`，在将每个参数对照相应的定义域检查之后，其类型为 `f` 的结果类型。单独的 lambda 无法推断（`CannotInferLambda`）。直接应用于参数的 lambda 的推断方式是：先推断第一个参数的类型，再在该假设下推断体的类型。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:170
msgid "`check` verifies a term against a type."
msgstr "`check` 将项对照类型进行检验。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:176
msgid "A lambda checks against an arrow type by checking its body against the codomain, with the parameter given the domain. Every other term is inferred and compared with `==`; a difference gives `TypeMismatch`."
msgstr "lambda 对照箭头类型进行检查时，会以定义域作为参数的类型，将体对照陪域进行检查。其他所有项都先推断类型，再用 `==` 比较；若不同则给出 `TypeMismatch`。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:199
msgid "[!WARNING] When a lambda is applied to two or more arguments, `infer` types the remaining arguments in a context that already contains the lambda's parameter. If one of those arguments mentions a free variable with the same name as the parameter, it is typed with the parameter's type. Rename the parameter, or apply the arguments one at a time, until this is fixed."
msgstr "[!WARNING] 当 lambda 被应用于两个或更多参数时，`infer` 会在已经包含该 lambda 参数的上下文中为其余参数确定类型。如果其中某个参数提到了与该参数同名的自由变量，它就会被赋予该参数的类型。在此问题修复之前，请重命名参数，或者逐个应用参数。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:206
#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:107
#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:158
msgid "Normalization"
msgstr "范式化"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:210
msgid "`normalize_checked` checks a term against a type and then normalizes it with the untyped beta-eta reducer."
msgstr "`normalize_checked` 将项对照类型进行检查，然后用无类型的 β-η 归约器对其范式化。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:217
msgid "On a type error it returns `Err` without reducing. Otherwise it returns `Ok(@lambda.normalize(term, max_steps))`: normal-order beta-eta reduction with a step limit. Its normal forms are beta-normal and eta-*short*."
msgstr "遇到类型错误时，它返回 `Err` 而不进行归约。否则返回 `Ok(@lambda.normalize(term, max_steps))`：带步数上限的正规序 β-η 归约。其范式是 β-范式且 η-*短*的。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:223
msgid "`normalize_eta_long` checks a term against a type and returns its beta-normal, eta-long form, computed by typed normalization by evaluation."
msgstr "`normalize_eta_long` 将项对照类型进行检查，并返回其 β-范式、η-长形式，该形式通过带类型的求值范式化计算得到。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:230
msgid "In the result, every subterm of arrow type is a lambda, and every application has a variable or a constant at its head. Variables of the context and constants of the signature are kept as they are and eta-expanded according to their types. No step limit is needed: well-typed terms always normalize. New binder names are `x`, `x_1`, … chosen to avoid every name of the term and the context."
msgstr "在结果中，每个箭头类型的子项都是 lambda，每个应用的头部都是变量或常量。上下文中的变量和签名中的常量保持原样，并按其类型进行 η-展开。不需要步数上限：良类型的项总能范式化。新的绑定子名称为 `x`、`x_1`、…，其选取会避开项和上下文中的所有名字。"

#: manual/api/stlc.md:266
msgid "The hidden method forms `not_equal` and `to_repr` on the types of this package are deprecated; use `!=` and `Repr(x)`."
msgstr "本包中各类型上隐藏的方法形式 `not_equal` 和 `to_repr` 已弃用；请使用 `!=` 和 `Repr(x)`。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:1
msgid "substitution API"
msgstr "substitution API"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:3
msgid "The `substitution` package replaces free variables by terms without capturing variables. `Substitution[T]` works on `@syntax.Term[T]`; `GenericSubstitution[N]` works on any AST that implements `@syntax.BindingSyntax`. Both are finite, simultaneous and immutable."
msgstr "`substitution` 包用项替换自由变量，且不会捕获变量。`Substitution[T]` 作用于 `@syntax.Term[T]`；`GenericSubstitution[N]` 作用于任何实现了 `@syntax.BindingSyntax` 的 AST。两者都是有限的、同时的且不可变的。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:16
msgid "The definition of capture-avoiding substitution and the proofs of its laws are in the [substitution design](../design/substitution.md)."
msgstr "避免捕获的代换的定义及其定律的证明见[代换设计](../design/substitution.md)。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:19
msgid "Substitutions on `Term`"
msgstr "`Term` 上的代换"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:23
msgid "`Substitution[T]` is a finite map from names to replacement terms."
msgstr "`Substitution[T]` 是从名字到替换项的有限映射。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:31
msgid "It denotes the map $\\sigma$ with $\\sigma(x) = s$ for an entry $(x, s)$ and $\\sigma(x) = x$ (the variable itself) for every other name. The entries are read-only outside the package; at most one entry exists per name."
msgstr "它表示映射 $\\sigma$：对于条目 $(x, s)$ 有 $\\sigma(x) = s$，对于其他所有名字有 $\\sigma(x) = x$（即变量本身）。这些条目在包外是只读的；每个名字至多有一个条目。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:37
msgid "These functions build substitutions."
msgstr "以下函数用于构建代换。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:45
msgid "`set(x, s)` adds $x \\mapsto s$, replacing an existing entry for `x` in place."
msgstr "`set(x, s)` 添加 $x \\mapsto s$，若 `x` 已有条目则就地替换。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:49
msgid "`Substitution::get` returns the replacement for a name, if any."
msgstr "`Substitution::get` 返回某个名字的替换项（如果有）。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:57
msgid "These methods shrink the domain of a substitution."
msgstr "以下方法用于缩小代换的定义域。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:64
msgid "`without(x)` drops the entry for `x`, which is what a binder for `x` does. `restrict(names)` keeps only the entries whose name is in `names`."
msgstr "`without(x)` 删除 `x` 的条目，这正是 `x` 的绑定子所起的作用。`restrict(names)` 只保留名字属于 `names` 的条目。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:84
msgid "`Substitution::apply` replaces the free variables of a term simultaneously, renaming binders to avoid capture."
msgstr "`Substitution::apply` 同时替换项中的自由变量，并重命名绑定子以避免捕获。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:91
msgid "Every free occurrence of a name `x` in the domain is replaced by its replacement; nothing is substituted inside an inserted replacement. Under `Bind(y, body)` the entry for `y` is ignored. When a replacement that is actually inserted into `body` has `y` free, the binder is renamed to a fresh name first, so free variables of replacements stay free. The result is determined up to the choice of fresh names, which is deterministic."
msgstr "定义域中名字 `x` 的每个自由出现都被替换为其替换项；不会在插入的替换项内部再做代换。在 `Bind(y, body)` 之下，`y` 的条目被忽略。当某个实际插入到 `body` 中的替换项含有自由的 `y` 时，会先将绑定子重命名为新鲜名字，从而替换项中的自由变量保持自由。结果在新鲜名字的选取意义下是确定的，而该选取本身是确定性的。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:112
msgid "`Substitution::then` composes two substitutions, applying `self` first."
msgstr "`Substitution::then` 复合两个代换，先应用 `self`。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:118
msgid "`s.then(t)` maps each `x` in the domain of `s` to `t.apply(s(x))`, and each other `x` in the domain of `t` to `t(x)`. For every term, `s.then(t).apply(term)` is alpha-equivalent to `t.apply(s.apply(term))`."
msgstr "`s.then(t)` 将 `s` 定义域中的每个 `x` 映射到 `t.apply(s(x))`，将 `t` 定义域中的其余每个 `x` 映射到 `t(x)`。对于每个项，`s.then(t).apply(term)` 与 `t.apply(s.apply(term))` α-等价。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:142
msgid "`from_renaming` turns a renaming into a substitution on a given set of names."
msgstr "`from_renaming` 将一个重命名转换为作用于给定名字集合上的代换。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:148
msgid "The result maps each listed name `x` with `renaming.apply(x) != x` to `Variable(renaming.apply(x))`. When the free variables of a term are among the listed names, applying the result is alpha-equivalent to `term.rename_free(renaming)`."
msgstr "结果将每个满足 `renaming.apply(x) != x` 的所列名字 `x` 映射到 `Variable(renaming.apply(x))`。当项的自由变量都在所列名字之中时，应用该结果与 `term.rename_free(renaming)` α-等价。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:165
msgid "Substitutions on binding-aware ASTs"
msgstr "感知绑定的 AST 上的代换"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:169
msgid "`GenericSubstitution[N]` is a finite map from names to nodes of a downstream AST `N`."
msgstr "`GenericSubstitution[N]` 是从名字到下游 AST `N` 的节点的有限映射。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:180
msgid "These functions build and query generic substitutions; they behave exactly like their `Substitution` counterparts."
msgstr "以下函数用于构建和查询泛型代换；它们的行为与对应的 `Substitution` 版本完全相同。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:193
msgid "`GenericSubstitution::apply_once` applies the substitution to a node in one simultaneous, capture-avoiding pass."
msgstr "`GenericSubstitution::apply_once` 以一趟同时且避免捕获的遍历将代换应用于节点。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:200
msgid "The algorithm is the one of `Substitution::apply`, run through `BindingSyntax::project` and rebuilt with `variable`, `apply` and `bind`. `Opaque` nodes are returned unchanged. \"Once\" means that inserted replacements are not visited again: substituting $x \\mapsto y$ and $y \\mapsto 2$ in $x + y$ gives $y + 2$, not $2 + 2$."
msgstr "算法与 `Substitution::apply` 相同，通过 `BindingSyntax::project` 执行，并用 `variable`、`apply` 和 `bind` 重建。`Opaque` 节点原样返回。“Once”的意思是不会再次访问插入的替换项：在 $x + y$ 中代换 $x \\mapsto y$ 和 $y \\mapsto 2$ 得到 $y + 2$，而不是 $2 + 2$。"

#: manual/api/substitution.md:217
msgid "On `Term[T]`, `apply_once` agrees with `Substitution::apply`. For a downstream AST see the [adapter tutorial](../tutorial/adapter.md)."
msgstr "在 `Term[T]` 上，`apply_once` 与 `Substitution::apply` 一致。关于下游 AST，请参阅[适配器教程](../tutorial/adapter.md)。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:1
msgid "syntax API"
msgstr "syntax API"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:3
msgid "The `syntax` package defines named syntax with binders: the generic term type `Term[T]`, the analyses on it (free variables, all names, alpha-equivalence), renaming, and the open trait `BindingSyntax` through which a downstream AST gets the same analyses and the generic substitution and rewriting of the other packages."
msgstr "`syntax` 包定义了带绑定子的命名语法：泛型项类型 `Term[T]`、其上的分析（自由变量、全部名字、α-等价）、重命名，以及开放 trait `BindingSyntax`——下游 AST 借助它获得同样的分析，以及其他包中的泛型代换与改写。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:16
msgid "The definitions behind these functions, and the proofs of their laws, are in the [syntax design](../design/syntax.md)."
msgstr "这些函数背后的定义及其定律的证明见[语法设计](../design/syntax.md)。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:19
#: manual/design/syntax.md:14
msgid "Terms"
msgstr "项"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:23
msgid "`Term[T]` is named syntax with domain values, variables, n-ary application and single-variable binding."
msgstr "`Term[T]` 是命名语法，包含领域值、变量、n 元应用和单变量绑定。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:35
msgid "`Value(v)` is a domain constant. Its payload `T` is opaque: it is treated as closed, so no analysis looks inside it."
msgstr "`Value(v)` 是领域常量。其载荷 `T` 是不透明的：它被视为闭合的，因此任何分析都不会查看其内部。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:37
msgid "`Variable(x)` is an occurrence of the name `x`."
msgstr "`Variable(x)` 是名字 `x` 的一次出现。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:38
msgid "`Apply(head, args)` applies `head` to a sequence of arguments. The lambda calculus packages read it as the curried application $head\\ a_1\\ \\cdots\\ a_n$."
msgstr "`Apply(head, args)` 将 `head` 应用于一串参数。lambda 演算相关的包将其解读为柯里化应用 $head\\ a_1\\ \\cdots\\ a_n$。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:41
msgid "`Bind(x, body)` binds `x` in `body`. In the lambda calculus it is $\\lambda x.\\,body$; a downstream language may read it as any one-variable binder."
msgstr "`Bind(x, body)` 在 `body` 中绑定 `x`。在 lambda 演算中它是 $\\lambda x.\\,body$；下游语言可以将其解读为任意单变量绑定子。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:45
msgid "`==` (`Term::equal`) is structural equality: binder names must match literally. Use `alpha_equal` to compare terms up to renaming of bound variables."
msgstr "`==`（`Term::equal`）是结构相等：绑定子名字必须字面一致。若要在约束变量重命名的意义下比较项，请使用 `alpha_equal`。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:63
msgid "`Term::equal` compares two terms structurally."
msgstr "`Term::equal` 按结构比较两个项。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:69
msgid "It is the promoted `Eq` implementation. `λx.x` and `λy.y` are not `equal`."
msgstr "它是提升而来的 `Eq` 实现。`λx.x` 与 `λy.y` 并不 `equal`。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:73
msgid "`Term::map_values` applies a function to every domain value and keeps the variables and binders."
msgstr "`Term::map_values` 对每个领域值应用一个函数，并保留变量和绑定子。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:80
msgid "It is a functor map: `t.map_values(v => v)` is `t`, and mapping `f` then `g` equals mapping `v => g(f(v))`. Free variables are unchanged."
msgstr "它是函子映射：`t.map_values(v => v)` 就是 `t`，先映射 `f` 再映射 `g` 等于映射 `v => g(f(v))`。自由变量保持不变。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:92
msgid "Analyses"
msgstr "分析"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:96
msgid "`free_variables` returns the names that occur free in a term."
msgstr "`free_variables` 返回在项中自由出现的名字。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:102
msgid "An occurrence of `x` is free when no enclosing `Bind(x, _)` binds it. Values contribute no names. Cost: $O(n)$ set operations for a term of size $n$."
msgstr "当没有外层的 `Bind(x, _)` 绑定 `x` 的某次出现时，该出现是自由的。值不贡献任何名字。代价：对大小为 $n$ 的项需要 $O(n)$ 次集合运算。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:107
msgid "`all_names` returns every name in a term: free variables, bound occurrences and binder names."
msgstr "`all_names` 返回项中的每个名字：自由变量、约束出现和绑定子名字。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:114
msgid "Use it as the \"used\" set when choosing a fresh name for a term."
msgstr "为项选取新鲜名字时，可将其用作“已使用”集合。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:132
msgid "`alpha_equal` decides whether two terms are equal up to the names of bound variables."
msgstr "`alpha_equal` 判定两个项在约束变量名字的意义下是否相等。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:139
msgid "Values are compared with `==`, free variables by name, and bound variables by the binder they refer to. The relation is an equivalence and is decided in one simultaneous traversal of both terms."
msgstr "值用 `==` 比较，自由变量按名字比较，约束变量按其所指的绑定子比较。该关系是等价关系，并通过对两个项的一趟同时遍历来判定。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:157
msgid "Renaming"
msgstr "重命名"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:161
msgid "`Term::rename_free` applies a renaming to the free variables of a term, renaming binders where necessary to avoid capture."
msgstr "`Term::rename_free` 对项的自由变量应用重命名，并在必要时重命名绑定子以避免捕获。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:168
msgid "Under `Bind(x, body)` the renaming loses its entry for `x`, because the bound `x` is a different variable. If a remaining target of the renaming equals `x`, the binder is renamed to a fresh name first. The result is alpha-equivalent to the textbook capture-avoiding renaming."
msgstr "在 `Bind(x, body)` 之下，重命名会失去 `x` 的条目，因为被绑定的 `x` 是另一个变量。如果重命名剩余的某个目标等于 `x`，会先将绑定子重命名为新鲜名字。结果与教科书中避免捕获的重命名 α-等价。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:186
msgid "`Term::alpha_rename_bound` renames the occurrences of a variable that are bound by an enclosing binder, refusing a target name that could be captured."
msgstr "`Term::alpha_rename_bound` 重命名被外层绑定子约束的某个变量的各次出现，并拒绝可能被捕获的目标名字。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:193
msgid "Call it on the *body* of a binder: `body.alpha_rename_bound(from, to_)` replaces the occurrences of `from` that are free in `body` (and therefore bound by the enclosing `Bind(from, body)`) with `to_`. Inner binders named `from` stop the renaming. The result is `None` when `to_` occurs anywhere in `body`, and `Some(body)` when `from == to_`. On success, `Bind(from, body)` and `Bind(to_, result)` are alpha-equivalent."
msgstr "请在绑定子的*体*上调用它：`body.alpha_rename_bound(from, to_)` 将 `from` 在 `body` 中自由（因而被外层 `Bind(from, body)` 约束）的出现替换为 `to_`。名为 `from` 的内层绑定子会阻止重命名。当 `to_` 出现在 `body` 中任何位置时结果为 `None`，当 `from == to_` 时结果为 `Some(body)`。成功时，`Bind(from, body)` 与 `Bind(to_, result)` α-等价。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:216
msgid "`BindingView[N]` is the one-layer view of a node that generic algorithms inspect."
msgstr "`BindingView[N]` 是泛型算法所检查的节点的单层视图。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:228
msgid "`Opaque` marks a node with no variables inside, such as a literal. The other cases mirror the constructors of `Term`, with the children left in the downstream type `N`."
msgstr "`Opaque` 标记内部不含变量的节点，例如字面量。其他情形与 `Term` 的构造器一一对应，子节点保留为下游类型 `N`。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:234
msgid "`BindingSyntax` is the open trait that a downstream AST implements to use the generic binding algorithms."
msgstr "`BindingSyntax` 是开放 trait，下游 AST 实现它即可使用泛型绑定算法。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:246
msgid "`project(node)` tells the algorithms what the node is."
msgstr "`project(node)` 告诉算法该节点是什么。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:247
msgid "`variable`, `apply` and `bind` rebuild nodes of each kind."
msgstr "`variable`、`apply` 和 `bind` 分别重建各类节点。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:249
msgid "An implementation must make `project` and the three constructors agree: `project(variable(x))` is `Variable(x)`, `project(apply(h, args))` is `Apply(h, args)`, `project(bind(x, b))` is `Bind(x, b)`, and rebuilding a projected `Apply` or `Bind` node gives back an equivalent node. An `Opaque` node must not contain variables. The [adapter design](../design/adapter.md) explains these laws; the [adapter tutorial](../tutorial/adapter.md) implements them for a small AST."
msgstr "实现必须使 `project` 与三个构造器保持一致：`project(variable(x))` 为 `Variable(x)`，`project(apply(h, args))` 为 `Apply(h, args)`，`project(bind(x, b))` 为 `Bind(x, b)`，并且重建一个投影得到的 `Apply` 或 `Bind` 节点会得到等价的节点。`Opaque` 节点不得包含变量。[适配器设计](../design/adapter.md)解释了这些定律；[适配器教程](../tutorial/adapter.md)为一个小型 AST 实现了它们。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:257
msgid "Call the trait methods through the trait, for example `@syntax.BindingSyntax::project(node)`."
msgstr "请通过 trait 调用 trait 方法，例如 `@syntax.BindingSyntax::project(node)`。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:262
msgid "`Term[T]` implements `BindingSyntax` with the obvious projection."
msgstr "`Term[T]` 以显然的投影实现了 `BindingSyntax`。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:268
msgid "`Value` projects to `Opaque` and every other constructor to the case of the same name, so the generic functions below agree with their `Term` versions on `Term` values."
msgstr "`Value` 投影为 `Opaque`，其他每个构造器投影为同名的情形，因此下面的泛型函数在 `Term` 值上与其 `Term` 版本一致。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:285
msgid "These functions compute free variables and all names for any `BindingSyntax` type."
msgstr "以下函数为任意 `BindingSyntax` 类型计算自由变量和全部名字。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:293
msgid "On `Term[T]` they return the same sets as `free_variables` and `all_names`."
msgstr "在 `Term[T]` 上，它们返回与 `free_variables` 和 `all_names` 相同的集合。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:297
msgid "`generic_alpha_rename_bound` is `Term::alpha_rename_bound` for any `BindingSyntax` type."
msgstr "`generic_alpha_rename_bound` 是适用于任意 `BindingSyntax` 类型的 `Term::alpha_rename_bound`。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:304
msgid "It returns `None` when the target name occurs in the node, and rebuilds the renamed node through `variable`, `apply` and `bind`."
msgstr "当目标名字出现在节点中时，它返回 `None`；它通过 `variable`、`apply` 和 `bind` 重建重命名后的节点。"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:324
msgid "`Term::variable(name)` method form"
msgstr "`Term::variable(name)` 方法形式"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:325
msgid "`Term::apply(head, args)` method form"
msgstr "`Term::apply(head, args)` 方法形式"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:326
msgid "`Term::bind(name, body)` method form"
msgstr "`Term::bind(name, body)` 方法形式"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:328
msgid "`Repr(term)` or `@debug.to_string(term)`"
msgstr "`Repr(term)` 或 `@debug.to_string(term)`"

#: manual/api/syntax.md:330
msgid "These method forms were implicit promotions of trait methods. They are kept hidden and deprecated so that old callers still compile."
msgstr "这些方法形式原本是 trait 方法的隐式提升。保留它们（隐藏且已弃用）是为了让旧的调用者仍能编译。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:1
msgid "utlc/lambda API"
msgstr "utlc/lambda API"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:3
msgid "The `utlc/lambda` package is the untyped lambda calculus over the shared named syntax `@syntax.Term[T]`: constructors for abstraction and application, the beta and eta rules, and a bounded normal-order normalizer. It is the reference operational semantics of the library."
msgstr "`utlc/lambda` 包是基于共享命名语法 `@syntax.Term[T]` 的无类型 lambda 演算：抽象与应用的构造器、β 规则与 η 规则，以及有界的正规序范式化器。它是本库的参考操作语义。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:17
msgid "The default alias is `@lambda`. In a lambda term, `Bind(x, b)` is $\\lambda x.\\,b$, `Apply(f, [a])` is $f\\,a$, and `Value(v)` is an opaque constant. The rules are explained in the [utlc/lambda design](../../design/utlc/lambda.md)."
msgstr "默认别名为 `@lambda`。在 lambda 项中，`Bind(x, b)` 是 $\\lambda x.\\,b$，`Apply(f, [a])` 是 $f\\,a$，`Value(v)` 是不透明常量。这些规则在 [utlc/lambda 设计](../../design/utlc/lambda.md)中有说明。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:22
msgid "Constructors"
msgstr "构造器"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:26
msgid "`abstraction` builds $\\lambda x.\\,body$."
msgstr "`abstraction` 构建 $\\lambda x.\\,body$。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:32
msgid "It returns `Bind(parameter, body)`."
msgstr "它返回 `Bind(parameter, body)`。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:36
msgid "`application` builds the unary application $f\\,a$."
msgstr "`application` 构建一元应用 $f\\,a$。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:42
msgid "It returns `Apply(function, [argument])`."
msgstr "它返回 `Apply(function, [argument])`。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:54
msgid "Rules"
msgstr "规则"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:58
msgid "`beta_rule` contracts a beta redex at the root of a term."
msgstr "`beta_rule` 收缩项根部的 β 可约式。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:64
msgid "For `Apply(Bind(x, body), [a, ..rest])` it returns the capture-avoiding substitution `body[x := a]`, applied to `rest` when `rest` is not empty. For every other term it returns `None`. It works for any domain type `T`, because values are never inspected."
msgstr "对于 `Apply(Bind(x, body), [a, ..rest])`，它返回避免捕获的代换 `body[x := a]`，当 `rest` 非空时再将其应用于 `rest`。对于其他所有项，它返回 `None`。它适用于任意领域类型 `T`，因为值从不被检查。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:71
msgid "`eta_rule` contracts an eta redex at the root of a term."
msgstr "`eta_rule` 收缩项根部的 η 可约式。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:77
msgid "For `Bind(x, Apply(f, [Variable(x)]))` with `x` not free in `f` it returns `f`; otherwise `None`. Only a unary application is an eta redex: `Bind(x, Apply(f, [a, Variable(x)]))` is not contracted."
msgstr "对于 `x` 在 `f` 中不自由的 `Bind(x, Apply(f, [Variable(x)]))`，它返回 `f`；否则返回 `None`。只有一元应用才是 η 可约式：`Bind(x, Apply(f, [a, Variable(x)]))` 不会被收缩。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:83
msgid "`beta_eta_rule` tries `beta_rule` and, if it does not apply, `eta_rule`."
msgstr "`beta_eta_rule` 先尝试 `beta_rule`，若不适用再尝试 `eta_rule`。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:89
msgid "A term cannot be both a beta and an eta redex at the root (one is an `Apply`, the other a `Bind`), so the order only documents priority."
msgstr "一个项不可能在根部既是 β 可约式又是 η 可约式（一个是 `Apply`，另一个是 `Bind`），因此顺序只是说明优先级。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:111
msgid "`normalize` reduces a term to beta-eta normal form with normal-order reduction, within a step limit."
msgstr "`normalize` 在步数上限内用正规序归约把项归约到 beta-eta 范式。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:118
msgid "It is `@eval.evaluate(term, \"beta_eta\", beta_eta_rule, NormalOrder, max_steps)`: at each step it contracts the leftmost-outermost beta or eta redex, anywhere in the term, including under binders. `NormalForm(t, n)` means `t` has no beta or eta redex (in the unary sense above) and was reached in `n` steps; `StepLimitReached` means the limit was used up. Divergent terms such as $\\Omega$ always end with `StepLimitReached`."
msgstr "它就是 `@eval.evaluate(term, \"beta_eta\", beta_eta_rule, NormalOrder, max_steps)`：每一步收缩项中任意位置（包括绑定子之下）最左最外的 beta 或 eta 可约式。`NormalForm(t, n)` 表示 `t` 没有 beta 或 eta 可约式（按上文的一元意义），且在 `n` 步内得到；`StepLimitReached` 表示步数上限已用完。发散项（例如 $\\Omega$）总是以 `StepLimitReached` 结束。"

#: manual/api/utlc/lambda.md:135
msgid "The first step is beta and produces $\\lambda y_1.\\,y\\,y_1$; the second is eta."
msgstr "第一步是 beta，得到 $\\lambda y_1.\\,y\\,y_1$；第二步是 eta。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:1
msgid "utlc/nbe API"
msgstr "utlc/nbe API"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:3
msgid "The `utlc/nbe` package normalizes untyped De Bruijn terms by evaluation: `eval` interprets a term in a lazy semantic domain, `quote` reads a semantic value back as a beta-normal term, and `normalize` does both. Every phase consumes *fuel*, so divergent terms end with `FuelExhausted` instead of running forever."
msgstr "`utlc/nbe` 包通过求值来范式化无类型 De Bruijn 项：`eval` 在惰性语义域中解释项，`quote` 把语义值读回为 beta 范式项，`normalize` 则两者都做。每个阶段都会消耗*燃料*，因此发散项以 `FuelExhausted` 结束，而不会永远运行下去。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:17
msgid "The default alias is `@nbe`. The semantic domain and the correctness argument are described in the [utlc/nbe design](../../design/utlc/nbe.md)."
msgstr "默认别名为 `@nbe`。语义域和正确性论证见 [utlc/nbe 设计](../../design/utlc/nbe.md)。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:20
msgid "Fuel"
msgstr "燃料"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:22
msgid "Fuel is a step budget measured in units: every evaluation of a term node, every forcing of a delayed value and every readback of a value costs one unit. All results report `consumed`, the units used. A call with fuel `<= 0` returns `FuelExhausted(consumed=0)` without doing anything (`quote` first rejects a negative level). The result of a call does not depend on the fuel beyond what it consumed: if a call with fuel $f$ returns a normal form after consuming $c$ units, every call with fuel at least $c$ returns the same result."
msgstr "燃料是以单位计量的步数预算：每次对项节点求值、每次强制延迟值、每次读回值都花费一个单位。所有结果都报告 `consumed`，即所用的单位数。燃料 `<= 0` 的调用不做任何事，直接返回 `FuelExhausted(consumed=0)`（`quote` 会先拒绝负的层级）。调用结果与超出其消耗量的燃料无关：若燃料为 $f$ 的调用在消耗 $c$ 个单位后返回范式，则任何燃料至少为 $c$ 的调用都返回相同的结果。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:31
msgid "Semantic values"
msgstr "语义值"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:35
msgid "`Semantic[T]` is an opaque semantic value."
msgstr "`Semantic[T]` 是不透明的语义值。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:45
msgid "A semantic value is a constant, a closure (a binder body with its environment), a delayed argument, or a neutral value (a free variable, a variable at a quote level, or a neutral value applied to an argument). The representation is private; values are produced by `eval` and the `reflect_*` functions and consumed by `quote`."
msgstr "语义值是常量、闭包（带有环境的绑定子体）、延迟参数或中性值（自由变量、某个 quote 层级上的变量，或作用于参数的中性值）。其表示是私有的；值由 `eval` 和 `reflect_*` 函数产生，由 `quote` 消费。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:53
msgid "`reflect_free` turns a free name into a neutral semantic value."
msgstr "`reflect_free` 把自由名转换为中性语义值。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:59
msgid "Quoting it gives `Free(name)`."
msgstr "对其 quote 得到 `Free(name)`。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:63
msgid "`reflect_level` turns a quote level into a neutral semantic variable."
msgstr "`reflect_level` 把 quote 层级转换为中性语义变量。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:69
msgid "Returns `None` for a negative level. Quoting the variable of level `l` at depth `n > l` gives `Bound(n - l - 1)`."
msgstr "层级为负时返回 `None`。在深度 `n > l` 处对层级 `l` 的变量 quote 得到 `Bound(n - l - 1)`。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:90
msgid "Evaluation and readback"
msgstr "求值与读回"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:94
msgid "`EvaluationResult[T]` is the outcome of `eval`."
msgstr "`EvaluationResult[T]` 是 `eval` 的结果。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:106
msgid "`eval` evaluates a closed De Bruijn term to weak head form in the lazy semantic domain."
msgstr "`eval` 在惰性语义域中把闭 De Bruijn 项求值为弱头形式。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:113
msgid "The term must be well scoped (free names are allowed); otherwise the result is `ScopeFailure` with `consumed=0`. Evaluation is call by name: arguments are delayed and evaluated only when needed, and evaluation stops at a closure or a neutral value without entering binders."
msgstr "项必须是良作用域的（允许自由名）；否则结果为 `ScopeFailure`，且 `consumed=0`。求值采用传名调用：参数被延迟，仅在需要时求值；求值在闭包或中性值处停止，不进入绑定子。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:120
msgid "`QuoteResult[T]` is the outcome of `quote`."
msgstr "`QuoteResult[T]` 是 `quote` 的结果。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:132
msgid "`quote` reads a semantic value back as a beta-normal De Bruijn term."
msgstr "`quote` 把语义值读回为 beta 范式的 De Bruijn 项。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:138
msgid "`quote(value, level, fuel)` reads `value` back under `level` binders. A closure is read back by applying it to a fresh variable of the current level and reading the result under one more binder; neutral applications are read back argument by argument, which forces delayed arguments. Use `level = 0` for values from `eval`. A negative `level`, or a level variable that is not below `level`, gives `ScopeFailure(NegativeIndex)`."
msgstr "`quote(value, level, fuel)` 在 `level` 个绑定子之下读回 `value`。闭包的读回方式是：把它作用于当前层级的一个新变量，再在多一层绑定子之下读回结果；中性应用逐个参数读回，这会强制延迟参数。对来自 `eval` 的值使用 `level = 0`。负的 `level`，或不小于 `level` 的层级变量，会得到 `ScopeFailure(NegativeIndex)`。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:162
msgid "`NbeResult[T]` is the outcome of `normalize`."
msgstr "`NbeResult[T]` 是 `normalize` 的结果。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:175
msgid "`normalize` computes the beta normal form of a well-scoped De Bruijn term within a fuel budget."
msgstr "`normalize` 在燃料预算内计算良作用域 De Bruijn 项的 beta 范式。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:182
msgid "It validates the term, evaluates it and quotes the result at level 0, with one shared budget. `NormalForm(t, c)`: `t` is the beta normal form, reached with `c` units. `FuelExhausted(c)`: the budget ran out; the term may diverge or may need more fuel. `ScopeFailure`: the input has a dangling or negative index."
msgstr "它校验项、对其求值并在层级 0 对结果 quote，三者共享同一预算。`NormalForm(t, c)`：`t` 是 beta 范式，用 `c` 个单位得到。`FuelExhausted(c)`：预算耗尽；该项可能发散，也可能需要更多燃料。`ScopeFailure`：输入含有悬空或负的索引。"

#: manual/api/utlc/nbe.md:188
msgid "Applications in the result are unary: a normal form $f\\,a\\,b$ is returned as `Apply(Apply(f, [a]), [b])`, while `@debruijn.normalize` keeps the n-ary spine `Apply(f, [a, b])` of the input. The two agree after spines are flattened."
msgstr "结果中的应用是一元的：范式 $f\\,a\\,b$ 以 `Apply(Apply(f, [a]), [b])` 返回，而 `@debruijn.normalize` 保留输入的 n 元脊 `Apply(f, [a, b])`。将脊展平后两者一致。"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:1
msgid "adapter design"
msgstr "adapter 设计"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:3
#: manual/design/core.md:3
#: manual/design/debruijn.md:3
#: manual/design/eval.md:3
#: manual/design/rewrite.md:3
#: manual/design/stlc.md:3
#: manual/design/substitution.md:3
#: manual/design/syntax.md:3
#: manual/design/utlc/lambda.md:3
#: manual/design/utlc/nbe.md:3
msgid "Design goal"
msgstr "设计目标"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:5
msgid "Downstream repositories have their own ASTs (polynomial expressions, numeric expression trees, typed cores) and should not have to convert them to `Term[T]` to get correct binding semantics. The adapter design fixes how such an AST connects to the shared algorithms through `@syntax.BindingSyntax`, what an implementation must guarantee, and how that guarantee is tested. The `adapter` package holds the reference contract test; it has no public API."
msgstr "下游仓库有自己的 AST（多项式表达式、数值表达式树、带类型的核心语言），不应为了获得正确的绑定语义而必须把它们转换为 `Term[T]`。adapter 设计规定了这样的 AST 如何通过 `@syntax.BindingSyntax` 接入共享算法、实现必须保证什么，以及如何测试这一保证。`adapter` 包包含参考契约测试；它没有公共 API。"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:12
#: manual/design/core.md:11
#: manual/design/debruijn.md:12
#: manual/design/eval.md:11
#: manual/design/rewrite.md:13
#: manual/design/stlc.md:12
#: manual/design/substitution.md:13
#: manual/design/syntax.md:12
#: manual/design/utlc/lambda.md:13
#: manual/design/utlc/nbe.md:14
msgid "Mathematical background"
msgstr "数学背景"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:14
msgid "Views"
msgstr "视图"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:16
msgid "Let $N$ be the downstream AST and"
msgstr "设 $N$ 为下游 AST，并设"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:22
msgid "the signature functor of binding syntax, whose summands are `Opaque`, `Variable`, `Apply` and `Bind` of `BindingView[X]`. An adapter consists of a *projection* (coalgebra) and *constructors* (a partial algebra):"
msgstr "为绑定语法的签名函子，其和项为 `BindingView[X]` 的 `Opaque`、`Variable`、`Apply` 和 `Bind`。一个 adapter 由一个*投影*（余代数）和若干*构造子*（部分代数）组成："

#: manual/design/adapter.md:31
msgid "The view laws"
msgstr "视图定律"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:33
msgid "For all names $x$, nodes $h, b, n$ and arrays $\\bar a$:"
msgstr "对所有名 $x$、节点 $h, b, n$ 和数组 $\\bar a$："

#: manual/design/adapter.md:46
msgid "(V1)–(V3) say that constructors build what the projection reports; (V4) says that rebuilding a projected node gives back an equivalent node ($\\equiv$ is the downstream notion of equality, often `==`); (V5) is the \"closed atom\" contract of `Opaque`; (V6) makes structural recursion through $\\pi$ terminate. Under (V1)–(V4), $\\pi$ restricted to non-opaque nodes and $\\kappa$ are mutually inverse, so $N$ minus its opaque nodes is isomorphic to one layer of binding syntax over $N$."
msgstr "(V1)–(V3) 说的是构造子构建出的正是投影所报告的内容；(V4) 说的是重建一个被投影的节点会得到等价的节点（$\\equiv$ 是下游的相等概念，通常是 `==`）；(V5) 是 `Opaque` 的“闭原子”契约；(V6) 使经由 $\\pi$ 的结构递归终止。在 (V1)–(V4) 下，$\\pi$ 限制在非 opaque 节点上与 $\\kappa$ 互逆，因此去掉 opaque 节点后的 $N$ 同构于 $N$ 之上的一层绑定语法。"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:54
msgid "Why the laws suffice"
msgstr "为什么这些定律就足够了"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:56
msgid "Every generic algorithm is defined by structural recursion through $\\pi$ and rebuilds with $\\kappa$. For each algorithm, the proof of its law for `Term[T]` in the [syntax](syntax.md) and [substitution](substitution.md) designs uses exactly two facts about `Term`: that pattern matching sees the constructors, and that constructors build those same nodes. (V1)–(V4) state these facts for $N$. (V5) justifies treating opaque nodes as having $\\mathrm{FV} = \\mathrm{names} = \\varnothing$, and (V6) gives well-founded induction. Hence, for a lawful adapter:"
msgstr "每个泛型算法都通过经由 $\\pi$ 的结构递归定义，并用 $\\kappa$ 重建。对每个算法，[syntax](syntax.md) 和 [substitution](substitution.md) 设计中关于 `Term[T]` 的定律证明恰好用到 `Term` 的两个事实：模式匹配能看到构造子，以及构造子构建的正是这些节点。(V1)–(V4) 对 $N$ 陈述了这些事实。(V5) 证明了把 opaque 节点视为 $\\mathrm{FV} = \\mathrm{names} = \\varnothing$ 的合理性，(V6) 给出良基归纳。因此，对于合法的 adapter："

#: manual/design/adapter.md:65
msgid "`generic_free_variables` and `generic_all_names` compute $\\mathrm{FV}$ and $\\mathrm{names}$ of the node read as binding syntax;"
msgstr "`generic_free_variables` 和 `generic_all_names` 计算把节点读作绑定语法时的 $\\mathrm{FV}$ 和 $\\mathrm{names}$；"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:67
msgid "`generic_alpha_rename_bound` satisfies the alpha step;"
msgstr "`generic_alpha_rename_bound` 满足 alpha 步；"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:68
msgid "`GenericSubstitution::apply_once` is simultaneous and capture-avoiding (Lemmas 1–3 of the substitution design);"
msgstr "`GenericSubstitution::apply_once` 是同时且避免捕获的（substitution 设计的引理 1–3）；"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:70
msgid "`generic_top_down_once` satisfies the one-redex contract and the normal-form lemma of the [rewrite design](rewrite.md)."
msgstr "`generic_top_down_once` 满足 [rewrite 设计](rewrite.md)中的单可约式契约和范式引理。"

#: manual/design/adapter.md:73
#: manual/design/core.md:109
#: manual/design/debruijn.md:96
#: manual/design/eval.md:73
#: manual/design/rewrite.md:70
