#: manual/tutorial/adapter.md:192
msgid "All calls project as `Apply`, and the operator travels in the head, so `apply(head, args)` can rebuild any call. If your AST has separate node kinds such as `Add(a, b)` and `Mul(a, b)`, give them a head that identifies the kind (as `Sym` does here); otherwise `apply` cannot know which node to rebuild."
